Ordered, growable handler queue (gateway patch for whatsmeow; applied by whatsmeow-patches/apply.sh).
Replaces the 2,048-slot channel between the frame reader and the handler loop (16 KiB per connection up front;
when full, handleFrame logged "Handler queue is full, message ordering is no longer guaranteed" and started one
goroutine per node). nodeQueue holds nothing while idle, grows during a burst, keeps strict FIFO order and
releases its memory once drained. Also updates the DangerousInternals wrappers that exposed the channel type.

